# Octofit Tracker Frontend Environment Configuration

## Codespaces Configuration

To run the frontend in GitHub Codespaces, you must define the `VITE_CODESPACE_NAME` environment variable.

### Setup Instructions

1. Copy this file to `.env.local` in the `octofit-tracker/frontend/` directory:

```bash
cp .env.example .env.local
```

2. Update `.env.local` with your Codespace name:

```
VITE_CODESPACE_NAME=your-codespace-name
```

### Finding Your Codespace Name

Your Codespace name is visible:
- In the browser URL: `https://your-codespace-name.github.dev`
- In GitHub Codespaces dashboard
- In VS Code (shown in the remote indicator)

### Running Locally

If `VITE_CODESPACE_NAME` is not defined, the frontend will automatically fall back to `http://localhost:8000`.

To run locally without Codespaces:
```bash
npm run dev
# The API will connect to http://localhost:8000
```

### Building for Production

```bash
npm run build
# The built app will use the configured API endpoint
```
